       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the usual maximum amlodipine dose, which is 10 mg once daily. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long, at about 30 to 50 hours, so the effects would last. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg PO once daily**, if you want a lower starting dose.\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
